      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Washington?",
      "a": "Washington received $13B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state has 80,705 awards and an average award size of $161K, and obligations fell 17.8% year over year. Historical totals were $15.6B in FY21, $12.1B in FY22, $13B in FY23, $15.4B in FY24, and $15.8B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Washington?",
